From 637fb09c6abefaa01515ef9244c4d000ad3f22b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yury Kirsanov <yury@kfi.net.au>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:42:53 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] hgstress: a multi-process shm allocator soak and
 fault-injection module

A test module, not for production, and excluded from the default build:
include it with include_modules= hgstress. Each worker churns shm cells of
sizes spanning every small class and the large tier, stamps every block
with its owner and verifies the stamps while the other workers churn, so a
cell handed to two owners shows up as torn words. MI commands park and
release stamped memory (to drive an elastic arena's grow and shrink) and
inject a double free or a scribbled free-list link, to check that the
allocator counts and survives them.

Works under any -a allocator; mem/README.hg_malloc_v3.md section 18
describes the runs.
